examples.translation:
His bells ring out, his large drums resound,
There are the three islands in the Huai;
Sad is my heart and moved.

[This] umbrageous sweet pear-tree;
Clip it not, hew it not down.
Under it the chief of Shao lodged.

There is the beautiful lady;
Tall and large, and majestic.
Waking or sleeping, I do nothing;
On my side, on my back, with my face on the pillow, I lie.

In the brook below the hill there drowns the orchid bud;
The sandy path between pine-trees shows not a trace of mud;
And cuckoos cry, in mournful rain.
